  "name": "Terminally Ill Adults (End of Life) Bill Committee",
  "parent_committee_id": null,
  "purpose": "<p>The&nbsp;Terminally Ill Adults (End of Life) Bill Committee was appointed to consider the safeguards and procedures contained in the Terminally Ill Adults (End of Life) Bill by hearing evidence including from professional bodies, those with professional experience of coronial services, and ministers.</p>\r\n<p>The Committee has concluded its work with the publication of its report, which included all oral and written evidence received. The Committee has now formally ceased to exist and so is unable to accept further evidence. The Bill is continuing its progress through the House:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://bills.parliament.uk/bills/3774\">Terminally Ill Adults (End of Life) Bill</a>.</p>",
